From a0b235b424c572e91a2aaca5eb2b328921cd9b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:13:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] service: don't send the SMIL part with a NUL terminator

The SMIL attachment of an outgoing message is given strlen() + 1 bytes,
so the part on the wire ends in a NUL octet that is not part of the
document. Receivers that hand the SMIL on as a string have to strip it:
mmsd4ofono added code to clean the SMIL it receives for exactly this,
naming mmsd-tng as the sender.

Send only the text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/service.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/service.c b/src/service.c
index 2662920..46212d1 100644
--- a/src/service.c
+++ b/src/service.c
@@ -1192,7 +1192,7 @@ send_message_get_args (GVariant           *parameters,
 
       attach->content_id = g_strdup (CONTENT_ID_SMIL);
       attach->content_type = g_strdup (CONTENT_TYPE_APP_SMIL);
-      attach->length = strlen (created_smil) + 1;
+      attach->length = strlen (created_smil);
 
       // Use safer g_memdup2() if glib is 2.68.1 or higher
 
-- 
2.53.0

